ullets curve  around buildings  and hit seemingly impossible targets  lady nagant also possesses a second  quirk that was given to her by all for  one  in order to help her complete her  mission to capture deku  this quirk is air walk which allows the  user to levitate through the air  as you can imagine being the world's  greatest long distance shooter and then  being able to fly through the air and  get a bird's eye view  on your opponent whenever you want is a  killer combination  and while i don't agree with hawks that  deku must run away from lady nagant  because she is too strong for him i  think that deku has proven otherwise  especially as he continues to master his  new quirks  i do think the lady nagant definitely  belongs in the top 5  strongest multiple quirk users in mha  at number four is none other than  deku as the ninth and current one for  all user  deco has the advantage of using the  quirk now that it is at its strongest  ever in fact deku inherited the quirk at  a crucial moment  in its evolution and as a result he is  able to manifest the original quirks of  all of the previous one for all users  in addition to being able to use one for  all itself and if that  wasn't enough all the additional quirks  that deku gets to unlock are even  stronger now than they were when they  were being used by their original users  and this is because a one for all's  growing strength has made these  additional quirks  even stronger as of the making of this  video deku has unlocked  black whip float danger sense smoke  screen  and fog in and not only has deku  unlocked these quirks but he has already  shown a truly impressive ability to  combine the different quirks in  extremely effective ways  in battle deku is learning quickly and  getting stronger with  each passing chapter and i'm sure that  eventually he will be able to climb his  way to the very top  of this list but for now he remains at  number  4. at number 3 we have  gigantomachia gigantomachia  is all for one's former bodyguard and  one of the strongest characters  in the entire series he is fiercely  loyal to his master  all for one and to his master's  successor tomura shigaraki  as his name suggests gigantomachia can  increase his size until he becomes a  genuine  giant and in this gigantic state  he can take down entire mountains and  entire city blocks  on his own on top of having insane and  utterly superhuman power  speed and stamina gigantomachia also has  at least  seven different quirks gigantomachia's  only known weakness is that he can  hardly  think for himself he requires orders  from his master  in order to carry out a task and the  only known task that he can accomplish  without being ordered to  is to come protect his master along with  being able to become  gigantic he can also completely block  out pain  he can convert his morale into stamina  he can enhance his senses  he can harden his muscles and he can  grow giant claws from his hands  and probably a lot more during the epic  war arc  it took literally dozens of heroes and  hero students to take  this man down and even then all they  could do is sedate him  he also managed to kill multiple pro  heroes in the process  while injuring many many others  gigantomachia's biggest weakness  is that he doesn't really have a will of  his own and unless he gets those direct  orders from his master or unless he  believes that he is acting to protect  his master  he isn't really a threat but at the same  time  when he does have the proper motivation  gigantomachia is a force of nature  he is a walking natural disaster and he  is  nearly unstoppable at number 2 we have  all for one all for one is the greatest  villain in the history of japan  and he is an absolutely ruthless  mastermind with an incredibly  overpowered quirk  all for one the quirk allows its user to  steal the quirks of others  and then use those quirks himself and  this includes combining multiple quirks  inside one person to create extremely  effective  offensive and defensive techniques all  for one can combine  multiple stolen quirks in order to  create more powerful super quirks that  would never have occurred  naturally and he was even able to slow  down the aging process  thanks to a quirk he copied from dr  ujiko all for one is able to forcibly  activate the quirks of others  and he can also transfer stolen quirks  into other people  allowing him to create his own army of  villains with super powered combo quirks  gigantomachia is of course one of all  for one's creations  as are the nomu all for one has  incredible intelligence  generations of experience and a  countless number of quirks  at his disposal not to mention the army  of multiple quirk users that he himself  is able to create  this makes him one of the strongest  characters in the entire series and the  second strongest multiple quirk user  in boku no hero now before we get into  the strongest multiple quark user  here are some honorable mentions first  up we have the third  one for all user i think that his  original quirk  fojin is such a good companion quirk to  one for all  fojin is basically a major buff for one  for all itself  you can use fojin to make your one for  all based attacks  much stronger and faster but with that  said  one for all itself was nowhere near as  strong back then  as it is now so that is why the third  user is an honorable mention  rather than being on the list himself  the same goes for all of the other  one for all users they were all strong  and they all deserve an honorable  mention  but i don't think that they quite make  the list based on their original quirks  and based on the strength of one for all  at the time i also want to give a quick  shout out to some of the villains from  the first two  mha movies including wolfram 9  and chimera who all used more than one  quirk  i chose not to include them on this list  not because they aren't strong enough to  be here  but because it is basically impossible  to power scale them in any meaningful  way  the movies are not really canon at least  not fully  and while there are some references to  characters from the movies in the actual  manga  there are also some clear  inconsistencies which make it impossible  to accurately compare the movie villains  to the canonical characters  finally i'd like to give an honorable  mention to shoto todoroki i didn't  include him on the list because he  technically has only one quirk  but that quirk consists of two  completely different powers that can be  used  separately so you could definitely make  an argument for shoto being a multiple  quirk user  also i guess monoma has potential but he  has a long way to go  and the absolutely strongest multiple  quirk user  at this point in the story is the  monster that is  awakened shigaraki in my opinion  shigaraki started out as a pretty  mediocre villain early on in the story  but over 300 chapters later he has  become an entirely different  person he is so much stronger now that  he was at the beginning that he is  essentially a totally different villain  don't get me wrong shigaraki has always  been very intelligent and  analytical and he's always had an  overwhelming hatred for the hero society  because of what he went through as a  child  this hatred imbued shigaraki with  incredible willpower  he will stop at nothing to destroy the  hero society  and this exceptional willpower is one of  the main reasons why  all for one took such a great interest  in shigaraki in the first place  after decades of trying to figure out a  way to steal one for all  all for one came to the conclusion that  one for all can in fact  be stolen but it can only be stolen by  someone with overpowering hatred  and unfathomable willpower someone who  can subdue the vestiges of the former  one for all users  and force the quirk to bend to his will  all for one believes that shigaraki is  the one who can make  this happen as i mentioned shigaraki has  undergone a massive transformation  over the past few arcs of the story a  transformation that is both physical  and psychological first he was able to  awaken the true power of his  quirk decay when we first meet him  shigaraki is able to only disintegrate  something that he touches with all five  of his fingers  and it took some time for that  disintegration to actually run its  course  but after his quirk awakened to its true  power  the decaying became instantaneous and it  could also spread beyond the person or  object that shigaraki was actually  touching directly the decay could now  spread to multiple enemies and destroy  them all at once and the quirk's ability  was further boosted after shigeraki  underwent ujjiko's body modifying  procedure  the procedure made shigaraki much  stronger physically and it also made him  capable of decaying  practically a third of an entire city  with one attack  shigaraki now also has more control of  his decay and he can seemingly decide  what he wants decayed and one he wants  spared  ujico's procedure has also drastically  increased shigaraki's speed and stamina  which is why he is now in a completely  different level of power than he was  before  but this is a list about multiple quirk  users  and ujiku's procedure had another  important effect it  transferred the original version of the  quirk all for one  on to shigaraki along with a bunch of  other quirks that the villain all for  one had stolen in the past  these quirks include super regeneration  ragdoll's former quirk  surge air cannon radio waves that red  tendril quirk known as rivet stab  and who knows how many more and despite  being a newly minted multiple quirk user  shigaraki has already demonstrated an  incredible ability to use these quirks  together  in order to fight multiple top tier  heroes on his own  to be fair fujiku's procedure was  interrupted before it could be completed  so the new shigaraki is not actually as  strong as he could have been  but he is still almost certainly the  strongest character  at this point in the story he can  destroy large  chunks of a city with a single attack he  can take on a large number of top tier  pro heroes  on his own and he has the potential to  become even stronger  if the villains can figure out a way to  complete ujico's procedure  there are several reasons why i believe  that shigaraki is even  stronger than all for one in his prime  this includes shigaraki's newly awakened  decay quirk which all for one did not  possess  it also includes the super regeneration  quirk which all for one only came across  after he was already permanently injured  by almighty  on top of that the procedure that ujico  conducted on shigaraki is far more  advanced than anything he could have  done for all for one back in all for  one's prime  and of course shigaraki's hatred and  willpower are presumably even greater  than all for once  because as we know all for one never  could find a way to steal one for all  himself  but he believes that shigaraki will be  able to do it now it is important to  mention that all for one's plan  is to perfect chicago's body and then  take it over from the inside  using all for one's work factor which  somehow retains  his own consciousness within it but  whether this plan succeeds or not  shigaraki is at this moment the  strongest multiple quirk user in the  story  and almost certainly the strongest  character in the story period  now let me know what you guys think do  you agree with this list  and if not no hard feelings just let me  know in the comments what your own list  would look like  if you enjoyed this pocono hero video  and you want to see more in the future  just leave a like and comment it only  takes a second but it really helps with  the youtube algorithm  and if you're new to the channel or  maybe you watch our videos but you  haven't taken the time to subscribe yet  do me a favor and make this the video  that you subscribe and  hit that no